"MG Baltic" case: Gustainis lawyer says that he has not yet got acquainted with the case-filed
The eleventh meeting of the MG Baltic case on Monday came all the defendants: Šarūnas Gustainis, Gintaras Steponavičius, Vytautas Gabšys, Eligijus Masiulis and Raimondas Kurlianskis.
The hearing began with the testimonial of the defendants.
At the last court hearing the state-appropriate Alexander Doroshev, the new attorney-appropriate of Gustainis, told the judicial panel that he did not get acquainted with the case.
L. Belevičius, a lawyer at MG Baltic, immediately stated that, in order to ensure a full-fledged human defence, a panel of judges had to allow the new lawyer to get acquainted with the case-file and asked to postpone the hearing.
"In order to ensure a person's defence, he/her must familiarize himself/herself with the materials of the criminal case.
It's not just a formal meeting," Belevičius said.
The new lawyer A. Dorošev noted that he did not get acquainted with the inquisitive act or the entire material of the case.
Before that, at the previous court hearing, the suspect Gustainis announced that he had renounced his lawyer because he would no longer be able to pay him.
Audio recordings were also listened to at the meeting.
Lawyers of the defendants revived that sound recordings submitted to the court were of poor quality.
Law enforcement suspects that the politicians, taking bribes from "MG Baltic", supported or initiated decisions favorable to the group in the Seimas and other state institutions, also had an impact on determining the violators of public procurators, ELTA recalls.
More than 150 persons were questioned during the pre-trial investigation, more than 50 of whom were members of the previous Seimas, several former ministers, members of the European Parliament.
More than 200 surveys and more than 30 searches were carried out.
It is suspected that Š. Gustainis received a bribe of more than 8 thousand euros, G. Steponavičius - 15 thousand euros, V. Gapšys - more than 27 thousand E. Masiulis is suspected of taking a bribe of more than 106 thousand euros.
The Labour Party is suspected of bribery and trade in influence, the Liberal Movement - bribery, trade in influence and abuse, and MG Baltic is suspected of bribing and trade in influence of these parties.
It is suspected that the politicians had been discussing the bribes with the vice-president R. Kurlianskis, the vice-president of MG Baltic, and later in the Seimas or in any other institutions offered or supported initiatives favourable to the concern.
Ethics watchdogs: The Board of the Liberal Sąjūdis is right about the actions of the Vilnius branch
