Researchers are advising the use of drones for animals to film responsibly, don't go too close, don't make noise and don't flies where it's forbidden.
Retired president appealed through the newspaper
Kyiv's court on Tuesday invited President Viktor Yanukovych, who retired to Russia, to come to the trial because of his alleged treason in an unusual manner - the convening was published in the official gazette of the state.
In a convoity interview published in the government newspaper Uriadovo Kurjer, the former leader is invited to appear at a hearing in criminal proceedings on November 19, in which his final arguments could be heard.
The document specifies that Yanukovych has the right to take part in the meeting by video link.
On Oct. 30, the Kiev court announced the completion of the debation in Yanukovych's case.
Yanukovych's lawyer Alexander Goroshinski, working in Russia, was given the opportunity to sign up until November 19 in the register of foreign lawyers so that he could take part in a meeting where Yanukovych is expected to speak his last word by video.
Yanukovych, supported by the Kremlin, was ousted and fled to Russia during the Maidan Uprising in February 2014, provoking the president's refusal to sign an association agreement with the European Union.
"Russian President Vladimir Putin later revealed that the former leader of Ukraine had been taken to Russia during a special operation organized by Moscow.
