"Following reclassification of this case into murder, they are quite righteous and justifiably and justifiably subject to life imprisonment," Ukraine's president said.
He righteously described the public's demand to openly and impartially announcing the case.
Poroshenko emphasized that statements by law enforcement officials in the parliament should show that "the government is determined to prominently bring criminals and killers to account, whoever they may be."
He also said that political speculation on the topic will not help to clarify the situation, but will further confuse everything.
"I am urinating all the forces of the government and the support of the opposition, do not squander unreasonable arguments and, God forbid, do not use this assassination for public relations," the president said.
"Conversely, now we need to unite and ensure that the investigation is effective, fair and transparent, fast - in such a way as to raise public confidence.
There's just no other way for us.'
"No one will be allowed to take advantage of this situation in destabilising the situation in the country," he said.
Handziuk, who struggled against corruption, was attacked and poured with an aerial acid in Kherson in the city of Kherson in July.
She was an adviser to the mayor of this southern Ukrainian city.
The woman was hospitalized after the attack but died in hospital on Sunday.
After the police and prosecutors did not address the perpetrators of the attack, Ukrainian Prosecutor General Yuri Lutsenko submitted his resignation on Tuesday.
