Over the next weekend, a new T1 shopping mall will be opened in the capital of Estonia, inflicted EUR 70 million into local real estate (NT) development company Pro Kapital Grupp.
130,000 sq. m of total, or 55,000 s sq. m rented, in the supermarket there will be 150 store services or entertainment venues, more than 30 cafés and restaurants, according to the developer's statement.
