"All the works are coordinated with heritage and other institutions," Sužeidėlis added, adding that the result would be the most authentic, but at the same time the practical side is also important - the canopigles must protect valuables from moisture.
A universal solution is chosen when working with heritage.
Before that, the elements of the Kaunas castle were covered with tin during the Soviet times, so they no longer had a historical value," the director of the Kaunas City Museum elaborated.
